# Round q38legs (D1b-a): Qwen3.8's card leg on the step. Same binary, two arms by the plan lever:
# BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=host (every routed expert on the host tier, today's 40.46 tok/s at depth 6,
# rig-log 09-28#q38-release) against =card (place::Experts::Card: each of the 43 eligible layers' id
# prefix on the card, 303 on the first 4 and 302 on the rest at ctx 4096, U 4096 — qwen4exp_meta's
# CARD_PLANS). Per layer the step is a sum across layers and a max inside one: card front 194 us (the
# mixes, mixer, router; C_front / 48) -> go -> [host bridge over the host slots || card shadow: shared
# expert 24 us + the leg's five launches 14 us + 5.3 us a card slot] -> wait -> combine. The leg sits
# under the host's window (the shadow passes the bridge only at K* >= 8..9 card slots of 10,
# P 0.04..0.15), so its own time is worth 0; the gain is the host's slots, 10 -> ~4.1 a layer at a
# card hit of 0.59 (uniform routing over 303/512). Step 24.72 ms -> 16.28..18.47 ms, 54.1..61.4
# tok/s, +34..+52 % [derived, q38d1bd §4, pred.py]. The hit a greedy continuation of the lcg prompt
# reaches is not measured: at h 0.20 / 0.30 / 0.45 the same model gives 44.3..45.8 / 46.5..49.0 /
# 50.2..54.8 tok/s, so the band is widened down to h 0.20: +9..+52 %.
# The runner pairs the two arms in one lease through q3arm's lever arms:
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38legs-tg.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4096' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp 6 6@BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=card.
# Wall [derived]: 2 arms x 2 rounds = 4 fresh processes, each a Qwen3.8 load of 40..90 s with the host
# set warm (the e2e gate's loads) plus its warm-up and ~2.5 s of 96 tokens, and the witness blocks: about
# 5..8 min; with a cold host set the first load reads ~111 GB at 2..3 GB/s, +40..60 s once. Under 30 min.
kind: ab
question: does the card leg shorten Qwen3.8's decode step by the host slots its card experts remove?
term: tg tok/s @ n=96, depth 6 (the lcg prompt), ctx 4096 (BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4096, so the card
  plan's ubatch is 4,096 and its counts are CARD_PLANS' row), A6000, plan a,
  BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=card against =host, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +9..+52
rounds: 2
condition: one binary, both arms through the lever in one lease, a fresh process per arm, the host
  set and the PLE table warm before each timed window (majflt in the window near 0), no [cpu-busy]
  or [other-busy] row; the card arm's plan line prints experts=card and card_experts 12,990 (4 x 303
  + 39 x 302), its load line card_layers=43; the host arm's plan line experts=host, card_experts 0
decide-in: land q38legs's plan lever as measured; run one untimed BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 card arm for
  the realized host slots a step (the card hit) and write it beside the tok/s in rig-log; open
  q38route (R2)
decide-below: read the realized card hit from one BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 run: a hit under 0.20 is the
  routing, not the leg (open the hot/adaptive placement question); a hit near 0.59 with the step
  still long means the leg left the host's window: nsys one card step before any change
decide-above: the host bridge's per-slot cost was over-counted: price it from the step stats' leg_us
  against host_slots before opening q38route
